    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "About",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Trained as an architect between Rome and Paris, Lorenzo Zandri chose to dedicate himself completely to photography and the process of the image in architecture — deciding not to build things, but images. His work oscillates between documentation and artistic expression, using photography to not only capture the built environment but also to evoke meaning, atmosphere, and cultural references. His approach is deeply rooted in visual storytelling, drawing on historical art imagery and analogies that enrich the narrative of space."
            ]
        }
